---
import { link } from "../../lib/url";
import fs from "node:fs";
import path from "node:path";
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";

// Read each area's validation report: the site is only built when both pass.
const areas = [
  { id: "budget", name: "Union Budget", sources: "/budget/sources/" },
  { id: "gdp", name: "GDP", sources: "/gdp/sources/" },
].map((a) => {
  const report = fs.readFileSync(path.resolve(process.cwd(), "..", a.id, "data", "validation_report.md"), "utf8");
  const m = report.match(/\*\*Result: (\w+)\*\* \(([\d,]+) checks, ([\d,]+) failures\)/);
  return { ...a, passed: m?.[1] === "PASSED", checks: m ? Number(m[2]) : 0 };
});
const total = areas.reduce((s, a) => s + a.checks, 0);
---
<Base title="About" description="What India Data Review is, where its numbers come from and how they are checked.">
  <h1>About India Data Review</h1>
  <p>
    India Data Review presents official data on India's economy and public finances: what the government budgets
    and spends, and how the economy grows. Every number is read by a program from the government's own documents
    and data services, kept with a fingerprint of the file it came from, and checked before the site is built.
  </p>

  <section class="card">
    <h2>Principles</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Official sources only.</strong> Budget documents (indiabudget.gov.in), MoSPI's national accounts, the Economic Survey and the Reserve Bank of India. No news reports, no estimates of our own.</li>
      <li><strong>Every figure traceable.</strong> Each number links back to the document or data release it came from; the downloaded files are kept with their SHA-256 fingerprints.</li>
      <li><strong>Checked automatically.</strong> {total.toLocaleString("en-IN")} checks across both areas{areas.every((a) => a.passed) ? ", all passing" : ""}. The site cannot be built if any fails. Problems found in the official data are listed with a reason, not hidden.</li>
      <li><strong>Nothing changed.</strong> The site picks, adds up and divides published figures, and says so wherever it does. Estimates are labelled as estimates.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <div class="grid-2">
    {areas.map((a) => (
      <section class="card">
        <h2>{a.name}</h2>
        <p>{a.checks.toLocaleString("en-IN")} checks, {a.passed ? "all passing" : "with failures"}.</p>
        <p><a href={link(a.sources)}>Sources, checks and problems found</a></p>
        <p class="small"><a href={link(`/data/${a.id}/validation_report.md`)}>Validation report</a></p>
      </section>
    ))}
  </div>

  <section class="card">
    <h2>Coming next</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Rural and urban indicators published every year: consumer prices, employment (PLFS), household spending (HCES).</li>
      <li>State GDP, from MoSPI.</li>
      <li>GDP revision history for 2000-01 to 2010-11, and IMF forecasts.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card">
    <h2>Earlier addresses</h2>
    <p class="muted">
      This site was India Budget Review (india-budget-review.k4tech.in). Old links still work: they redirect to the
      same page under <a href={link("/budget/")}>/budget/</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
